{"kind":"table","sheet":"Sheet1","address":"A1:B11","rows":11,"cols":2,"values":[["DRAFT CFS #2 QUESTIONS AND FEEDBACK",null],[null,null],[null,null],["PAGE # REFERENCE FROM DRAFT CFS #2","QUESTIONS/FEEDBACK FROM INDUSTRY"],["Pages 5 and 7","The draft requires a complete enterprise-cloud and tactical-edge continuum, states that partial solutions will not be considered, and also requires independently modular components. Will the final CfS permit a prime-led team to identify and separately demonstrate modular subcontractor capabilities? If so, will the Government publish a teaming or capability-exchange mechanism so qualified small businesses can participate without representing that they can deliver the full continuum alone?"],["Page 6","For Configuration Management, Data Logging/Alerting, and the Common Data Layer, will the final CfS define minimum machine-readable provenance artifacts? Recommended elements are source identity, schema and transformation lineage, software/model/configuration versions, timestamps, operator actions, exception states, and cryptographic hashes sufficient to reproduce or independently audit a result."],["Pages 7-8","Will the Vulcan submission instructions allow a compact machine-readable evidence manifest or supporting validation appendix outside the 10-page Technical Volume? If yes, please specify permitted formats, file-size limits, whether appendix pages count toward the limit, and whether links to externally hosted evidence will be evaluated."],["Pages 8-10","The initial White Paper requires binding not-to-exceed catalog ceilings before the final CfS and full Section 4 details are available. May vendors state explicit data-volume, security-domain, edge-hardware, hosting, and integration assumptions and provide modular ceiling prices that are revised downward after Government clarification without being treated as noncompliant?"],["Pages 10-11","For scientific, technological, or subject-matter-expert peer review, will the Government publish the evaluation metrics, acceptance thresholds, weighting, tie-breaking rules, and failure-handling rules before demonstrations? A pre-declared scorecard would make capability comparisons reproducible and reduce the risk of post-hoc metric substitution."],["Page 11 and Product Demonstration Plan","Will each invited vendor receive identical frozen Government-furnished datasets and task definitions, with a blind holdout portion reserved for evaluation? Please clarify how missing, malformed, delayed, or conflicting data will be logged and scored, and whether the Government will retain a hash manifest of all evaluation inputs and outputs."],["Page 15","For independently developed commercial software used to validate, route, or audit Government data, will the final CfS distinguish Government ownership of customer data from vendor ownership of pre-existing software, algorithms, and generic evidence-manifest schemas? Please clarify whether delivery of reproducible outputs and interface documentation can satisfy evaluation needs without transfer of underlying source code or privately funded technical data."]]}
